KZ3 patch 2203 (rsx night P0): the perf split no longer adds phantom time to the decode bucket (diagnostic, default off).
With RSX_PERF_SPLIT=1 RSX_O0=1 every method word paid a QPC push/pop pair in ld_dispatch_timed, two lock xadd O0 counters
and a per-command meth_t0 QPC pair (about 5-7 ms per flip). Now: (1) decode_d is timed on 1 word in 32 and its self time
scaled by 32 (taken from the bucket that owned the clock, so the buckets still add up to the walk; the credit goes to decode_d at once, the debit is applied at the pass end, clamped to what
the bucket accumulated (rest owed to later passes), so no per-flip bucket prints negative); the sampler phase persists across
walk passes (a per-pass phase never sampled a pass of 31 words or fewer); (2) the O0 m3d and
m3d_legacy counters are pass-local plain adds flushed at the pass end; (3) the meth_t0 pair is skipped while the split is
active. New line [perf-split-cost] (words, commands, timed words per flip). Everything is behind g_rsx_split_act and
g_rsx_o0.on: with the switches off the walker runs the same code as before (one int test per word, as in 2188).
Host test: tools/smoke/test_perf_split_cost.sh.
